        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ac750ee8-9a84-51cc-88fb-6a95a0a96ea2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Dhool, Ranja, Rajaputhran\n- People: Dharani, Vikram, Jyothika, Reemma Sen, Vivek, Sayaji Shinde, Telangana Sakunthala, Pasupathy, Sudesh Wasantha Peiris, Sunil T. Fernando, Suresh Gopi, Shobana, Murali\n- Companies: Sunil T. Films\n- Roles: actor, director, producer\n- Awards: Filmfare Awards, National Film Award, Tamil Nadu State Film Award, Honorary Doctorate\n- Organizations: People's University of Milan\n\nFacts:\n- Dhool is a 2003 Indian Tamil-language action masala film directed by Dharani.\n- Dhool stars Vikram, Jyothika, and Reemma Sen in lead roles, with Vivek, Sayaji Shinde, Telangana Sakunthala, and Pasupathy in supporting roles.\n- Rajaputhran stars Suresh Gopi, Vikram, Shobana, and Murali in lead roles.\n- In May 2011, Vikram was awarded an Honorary Doctorate by the People's University of Milan.\n- Vikram, whose professional name is Chiyaan Vikram, is an Indian film actor who predominantly appears in Tamil-language films.\n- Vikram has won seven Filmfare Awards, one National Film Award, and one Tamil Nadu State Film Award among other recognitions.\n- Ranja is a 2014 Sri Lankan Sinhala action thriller film directed by Sudesh Wasantha Peiris and produced by Sunil T. Fernando for Sunil T. Films.\n- Ranja is a remake of the 2003 Tamil-language film Dhool.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b3da231b-e321-5c1c-9ff9-9425ab5ec9a2",
        "text": "Page: Dhool. Sentence: Dhool (English: Super ) is a 2003 Indian Tamil-language action masala film directed by Dharani.\nPage: Dhool. Sentence: The film featured Vikram, Jyothika and Reemma Sen in the lead roles, while Vivek, Sayaji Shinde, Telangana Sakunthala and Pasupathy among others play supporting roles.\nPage: Vikram (actor). Sentence: Kennedy John Victor, known professionally as Vikram or Chiyaan Vikram, is an Indian film actor who predominantly appears in Tamil language films and has won seven Filmfare Awards as well as one National Film Award and Tamil Nadu State Film Award amongst other recognitions and was awarded an Honorary Doctorate by the People's University of Milan in May 2011.\nPage: Ranja. Sentence: Ranja (Sinhalese: \"රන්ජා\" ) is a 2014 Sri Lankan Sinhala action thriller film directed by Sudesh Wasantha Peiris and produced by Sunil T. Fernando for Sunil T. Films.It was the remake of 2003 Tamil language film Dhool.\nPage: Rajaputhran. Sentence: It stars Suresh Gopi, Vikram, Shobana and Murali and in the lead roles.",
